e trauma history or C8/T1 dermatomal patterns", "Diabetic mononeuropathy: Could explain unilateral symptoms but is less likely with concurrent pain and constitutional features"], "alarm_features": ["17 pound weight loss in 1 month", "Heavy alcohol consumption (2-7 drinks/day)", "Smoking 40 pack-years with apical risk implications"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Thoracic Malignancy with Neural Compression", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4242424242424243, "posterior": 0.3680911877130756, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute progression is atypical for embolic stroke and more consistent with inflammatory/malignant processes.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "evidence_against": ["No definitive signs of SVC syndrome or Cushingoid features observed, reducing but not eliminating concern for apical tumor."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of apical lung symptoms (cough, hoarseness)?", "Presence of superior vena cava syndrome?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Chest imaging (CT/MRI)", "Serum cancer markers"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neuromuscular Disorder of the Upper Extremity", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.05423740486931369, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of positional variation supports chronic processes over reactive mechanisms, moderately weakening B2 while having minimal impact on malignancy (B1) hypotheses."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Compression Syndrome of the Thoracic Outlet", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.24242424242424243, "posterior": 0.08953476359378768, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Fixed deficits with subacute onset are more characteristic of neurovascular compression (TOS) than isolated reactive nerve injury."], "evidence_against": ["Stable symptoms with head/neck movement and no anatomical risk markers (trauma, anomalies) contradict typical arterial TOS features.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of neck/shoulder trauma or anatomic anomalies?", "Pain changes with arm movement or scalenus muscle contraction?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Doppler ultrasound of subclavian artery", "Angiography of cervical/thoracic vessels"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Subacute Neurological Process with Ischemic Potential", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.018079134956437898, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Systemic Inflammatory/Reactive Nerve Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.07231653982575159, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Apical Lung Tumor with Truncal Compression (e.g., Pancoast Tumor)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.32542442921588216, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of SVC syndrome signs contradicts a chronic apical lung presentation, slightly downgrading B1.1 while neutral for the broader B1 category since parietal mechanisms remain possible."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Mediastinal Lymphadenopathy from Lymphoma (Non-Hodgkin’s/Other)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.08484848484848487, "posterior": 0.02531078893901306, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Weight loss alone (even in a steroid user) is insufficient to maintain high lymphoma suspicion without accompanying systemic symptoms. This weakens but does not completely rule out lymphoma as a consideration.", "Lack of constitutional symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma as the primary cause, moderately weakening B1.2 while having no material effect on B1.1 or other branches."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats, weight loss) consistent with lymphoma?", "History of prior lymphoproliferative illness?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Biopsy of enlarged mediastinal lymph nodes", "Flow cytometry of bone marrow aspirate"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Metastatic Thoracic Lesion (e.g., Neuroendocrine/Prostatic/Other)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.01735596955818038, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Anabolic steroid use, while not a direct carcinogen, weakens the metastatic lesion hypothesis due to lack of documented primary tumor sites in the patient history."]}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Scalenus Anticus Syndrome (Anatomical Variant Type)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03443644753607219, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Unreproducible scalenus signs (head-turning) contradict the expected clinical features of B3.1, but do not rule out the broader thoracic outlet family (B3) given uncertainty about anatomical variant subtypes."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Subclavian Steal Syndrome (True Neurovascular Type)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.02066186852164331, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of arm-elevation exacerbation (expected for B3.2) moderately weakens this diagnosis but preserves overall vascular compression (B3) plausibility through other subtypes."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "Thoracic Outlet Syndrome (Non-specific/Combined Type)", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.05772005772005773, "posterior": 0.03443644753607219, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Steroid use does not explain neurogenic TOS, and the absence of positional variation weakens this mechanism. Neurogenic TOS (B3.3) receives neutral effect due to inconsistent presentation patterns."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Pattern of weakness following medial/lateral arm distributions?", "History of brachial plexus injury or repetitive overhead trauma?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Dynamic ultrasound of all three TOS variants (neurogenic, venous, arterial)", "CT angiography with contrast during arm elevation"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.7, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.35, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}}, "frontier": ["B1.2", "B3.3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the patient’s hypertension and diabetes provide sufficient vascular risk to justify subclavian steal syndrome despite the lack of positional evidence?", "result_summary": "Vascular risk factors (hypertension, diabetes) provide moderate plausibility for subclavian steal (B3.2) but require positional evidence to confirm. The absence of this feature weakens but doesn't definitively rule it out.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.2": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 6, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of clinical signs such as radiating pain, hoarseness, or superior mediastinal syndrome in the vignette rule out an apical lung tumor as the causal mechanism of neural compression?", "result_summary": "Absence of SVC syndrome signs contradicts a chronic apical lung presentation, slightly downgrading B1.1 while neutral for the broader B1 category since parietal mechanisms remain possible.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "moderate_against", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.1": "neutral", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 7, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are there definitively documented lymphoproliferative symptoms (e.g., fevers, night sweats) in the patient history that would support mediastinal lymphoma rather than apical lung tumor?", "result_summary": "Lack of constitutional symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma as the primary cause, moderately weakening B1.2 while having no material effect on B1.1 or other branches.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "moderate_against", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.1": "neutral", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 8, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the absence of viral/autoimmune triggers and presence of positional stability in symptoms contradict isolated reactive nerve injury as the mechanism?", "result_summary": "The absence of positional variation supports chronic processes over reactive mechanisms, moderately weakening B2 while having minimal impact on malignancy (B1) hypotheses.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "neutral", "B3.1": "neutral", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 9, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of reproducible pain with neck motion directly contradict the expected clinical features of scalenus anticus syndrome in weightlifters?", "result_summary": "Unreproducible scalenus signs (head-turning) contradict the expected clinical features of B3.1, but do not rule out the broader thoracic outlet family (B3) given uncertainty about anatomical variant subtypes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.1": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 10, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented symptom exacerbation with arm elevation contradict the typical presentation of subclavian steal syndrome?", "result_summary": "Absence of arm-elevation exacerbation (expected for B3.2) moderately weakens this diagnosis but preserves overall vascular compression (B3) plausibility through other subtypes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.2": "moderate_against", "B3.1": "neutral"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.4242424242424243, "B2": 0.18181818181818182, "B3": 0.24242424242424243, "B4": 0.030303030303030307, "B5": 0.12121212121212123, "B1.1": 0.30303030303030304, "B1.2": 0.08484848484848487, "B1.3": 0.03636363636363636, "B3.1": 0.11544011544011545, "B3.2": 0.06926406926406926, "B3.3": 0.05772005772005773}, {"B1": 0.3680911877130756, "B2": 0.05423740486931369, "B3": 0.08953476359378768, "B4": 0.018079134956437898, "B5": 0.07231653982575159, "B1.1": 0.32542442921588216, "B1.2": 0.02531078893901306, "B1.3": 0.01735596955818038, "B3.1": 0.03443644753607219, "B3.2": 0.02066186852164331, "B3.3": 0.03443644753607219}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Patient's vitals are stable without acute hemodynamic instability, airway compromise, or severe respiratory distress. Neurological deficit is subacute (progression over weeks) and non-progressive (no acute stroke pattern). Constitutional symptoms (weight loss, smoking history, steroid use) suggest chronic pathologies requiring diagnostic evaluation rather than emergent stabilization.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch (B1.1) has posterior 0.325 < 0.75, and dangerous alternatives (B1.1) remain unresolved. Info_exhaustion conditions are not met as critical discriminators (chest imaging, Doppler ultrasound) are unexecuted."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.8, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.32542442921588216, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 55-year-old male bodybuilder presents to the emergency department with weakness of his right arm. The patient states he has experienced these symptoms for a few weeks; however, today his hand felt so weak he dropped his cup of tea. The patient has a medical history of diabetes. He drinks 2-7 alcoholic drinks per day and has smoked 2 packs of cigarettes per day since he was 25. The patient uses anabolic steroids. He has lost 17 pounds since he last came to the emergency department 1 month ago. His temperature is 99.5°F (37.5°C), blood pressure is 177/108 mmHg, pulse is 90/min, respirations are 17/min, and oxygen saturation is 98% on room air. Physical exam reveals decreased sensation in the right arm and 2/5 strength in the right arm and 5/5 strength in the left arm. The patient states that he is experiencing a dull aching and burning pain in his right arm during the exam. Symptoms are not changed with changes in head and neck position.", "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Apical lung tumor"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Brachial plexopathy"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Cerebral infarction"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Scalenus anticus syndrome"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Subclavian steal syndrome"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "content": "Age and gender: 55-year-old male", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E2", "kind": "direct", "content": "Occupation: bodybuilder", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E3", "kind": "direct", "content": "Chief complaint: weakness of right arm for several weeks", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E4", "kind": "direct", "content": "Today's event: dropped tea due to right hand weakness", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E5", "kind": "direct", "content": "Medical history: diabetes", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "meta