e trauma history or C8/T1 dermatomal patterns", "Diabetic mononeuropathy: Could explain unilateral symptoms but is less likely with concurrent pain and constitutional features"], "alarm_features": ["17 pound weight loss in 1 month", "Heavy alcohol consumption (2-7 drinks/day)", "Smoking 40 pack-years with apical risk implications"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Thoracic Malignancy with Neural Compression", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3680911877130756, "posterior": 0.349872224619163, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute progression is atypical for embolic stroke and more consistent with inflammatory/malignant processes.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "evidence_against": ["No definitive signs of SVC syndrome or Cushingoid features observed, reducing but not eliminating concern for apical tumor."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of apical lung symptoms (cough, hoarseness)?", "Presence of superior vena cava syndrome?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Chest imaging (CT/MRI)", "Serum cancer markers"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neuromuscular Disorder of the Upper Extremity", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.052271746706050254, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of positional variation supports chronic processes over reactive mechanisms, moderately weakening B2 while having minimal impact on malignancy (B1) hypotheses."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Compression Syndrome of the Thoracic Outlet", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.08953476359378768, "posterior": 0.06969566227473367, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Fixed deficits with subacute onset are more characteristic of neurovascular compression (TOS) than isolated reactive nerve injury."], "evidence_against": ["Stable symptoms with head/neck movement and no anatomical risk markers (trauma, anomalies) contradict typical arterial TOS features.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of neck/shoulder trauma or anatomic anomalies?", "Pain changes with arm movement or scalenus muscle contraction?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Doppler ultrasound of subclavian artery", "Angiography of cervical/thoracic vessels"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Subacute Neurological Process with Ischemic Potential", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.017423915568683418, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Systemic Inflammatory/Reactive Nerve Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06969566227473367, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Apical Lung Tumor with Truncal Compression (e.g., Pancoast Tumor)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.3136304802363015, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of SVC syndrome signs contradicts a chronic apical lung presentation, slightly downgrading B1.1 while neutral for the broader B1 category since parietal mechanisms remain possible."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Mediastinal Lymphadenopathy from Lymphoma (Non-Hodgkin’s/Other)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.02531078893901306, "posterior": 0.019514785436925433, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Lack of constitutional symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma as the primary cause, moderately weakening B1.2 while having no material effect on B1.1 or other branches.", "No direct evidence definitively excludes B1.2 lymphoma; the absence of systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma suspicion but does not eliminate the malignant process (B1)"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats, weight loss) consistent with lymphoma?", "History of prior lymphoproliferative illness?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Biopsy of enlarged mediastinal lymph nodes", "Flow cytometry of bone marrow aspirate"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Metastatic Thoracic Lesion (e.g., Neuroendocrine/Prostatic/Other)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.01672695894593608, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Anabolic steroid use, while not a direct carcinogen, weakens the metastatic lesion hypothesis due to lack of documented primary tumor sites in the patient history."]}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Scalenus Anticus Syndrome (Anatomical Variant Type)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.033188410607016036, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Unreproducible scalenus signs (head-turning) contradict the expected clinical features of B3.1, but do not rule out the broader thoracic outlet family (B3) given uncertainty about anatomical variant subtypes."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Subclavian Steal Syndrome (True Neurovascular Type)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.019913046364209618, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of arm-elevation exacerbation (expected for B3.2) moderately weakens this diagnosis but preserves overall vascular compression (B3) plausibility through other subtypes."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "Thoracic Outlet Syndrome (Non-specific/Combined Type)", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.03443644753607219, "posterior": 0.016594205303508018, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The fixed neurological deficit without positional variation does not provide strong evidence for B3.3 over specific anatomic subtypes like B3.2, which would typically require positional testing confirmation.", "Absence of typical injury patterns for B3.3 provides weak evidence against this mechanism but does not entirely exclude the broader thoracic outlet syndrome (B3) family given anatomic variant subtypes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Pattern of weakness following medial/lateral arm distributions?", "History of brachial plexus injury or repetitive overhead trauma?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Dynamic ultrasound of all three TOS variants (neurogenic, venous, arterial)", "CT angiography with contrast during arm elevation"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.7, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.35, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classifica