e trauma history or C8/T1 dermatomal patterns", "Diabetic mononeuropathy: Could explain unilateral symptoms but is less likely with concurrent pain and constitutional features"], "alarm_features": ["17 pound weight loss in 1 month", "Heavy alcohol consumption (2-7 drinks/day)", "Smoking 40 pack-years with apical risk implications"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Thoracic Malignancy with Neural Compression", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3680911877130756, "posterior": 0.349872224619163, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute progression is atypical for embolic stroke and more consistent with inflammatory/malignant processes.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "evidence_against": ["No definitive signs of SVC syndrome or Cushingoid features observed, reducing but not eliminating concern for apical tumor."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of apical lung symptoms (cough, hoarseness)?", "Presence of superior vena cava syndrome?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Chest imaging (CT/MRI)", "Serum cancer markers"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neuromuscular Disorder of the Upper Extremity", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.05423740486931369, "posterior": 0.052271746706050254, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Steroid use complicates paraneoplastic diagnosis without documented autoimmune features. This creates a neutral effect for B2 as reactive nerve injury (B5) remains an unconsidered alternative.", "The absence of positional variation supports chronic processes over reactive mechanisms, moderately weakening B2 while having minimal impact on malignancy (B1) hypotheses."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Trauma or repetitive strain causing brachial plexus injury?", "Recent viral illness or autoimmune triggers?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["EMG/NCS of upper extremity", "MRI brachial plexus"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Compression Syndrome of the Thoracic Outlet", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.08953476359378768, "posterior": 0.06969566227473367, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Fixed deficits with subacute onset are more characteristic of neurovascular compression (TOS) than isolated reactive nerve injury."], "evidence_against": ["Stable symptoms with head/neck movement and no anatomical risk markers (trauma, anomalies) contradict typical arterial TOS features.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of neck/shoulder trauma or anatomic anomalies?", "Pain changes with arm movement or scalenus muscle contraction?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Doppler ultrasound of subclavian artery", "Angiography of cervical/thoracic vessels"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Subacute Neurological Process with Ischemic Potential", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.017423915568683418, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Systemic Inflammatory/Reactive Nerve Disease", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.07231653982575159, "posterior": 0.06969566227473367, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Systemic inflammatory symptoms (fever, rash)?", "Recent surgery or infections? (e.g., brachial artery catheterization)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Serum protein electrophoresis", "Autoimmune panel"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "pathogenesis"}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Apical Lung Tumor with Truncal Compression (e.g., Pancoast Tumor)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.32542442921588216, "posterior": 0.3136304802363015, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The presence of 17 pounds of weight loss, a history of anabolic steroid use for bodybuilding, and subacute progression provides moderate support for apical lung tumor/parietal syndrome, though confidence in exclusion of alternatives remains low."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of SVC syndrome signs contradicts a chronic apical lung presentation, slightly downgrading B1.1 while neutral for the broader B1 category since parietal mechanisms remain possible."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of radiating arm pain or shoulder involvement?", "Cyanotic or edematous skin changes (superior mediastinal extension)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["High-resolution chest CT for apical mass with contrast", "PET scan for metabolic activity in parietacal space"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Mediastinal Lymphadenopathy from Lymphoma (Non-Hodgkin’s/Other)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.019514785436925433, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No direct evidence definitively excludes B1.2 lymphoma; the absence of systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma suspicion but does not eliminate the malignant process (B1)"]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Metastatic Thoracic Lesion (e.g., Neuroendocrine/Prostatic/Other)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.01672695894593608, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Anabolic steroid use, while not a direct carcinogen, weakens the metastatic lesion hypothesis due to lack of documented primary tumor sites in the patient history."]}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Scalenus Anticus Syndrome (Anatomical Variant Type)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.033188410607016036, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Unreproducible scalenus signs (head-turning) contradict the expected clinical features of B3.1, but do not rule out the broader thoracic outlet family (B3) given uncertainty about anatomical variant subtypes."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Subclavian Steal Syndrome (True Neurovascular Type)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.019913046364209618, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of arm-elevation exacerbation (expected for B3.2) moderately weakens this diagnosis but preserves overall vascular compression (B3) plausibility through other subtypes."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "Thoracic Outlet Syndrome (Non-specific/Combined Type)", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.03443644753607219, "posterior": 0.016594205303508018, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The fixed neurological deficit without positional variation does not provide strong evidence for B3.3 over specific anatomic subtypes like B3.2, which would typically require positional testing confirmation.", "Absence of typical injury patterns for B3.3 provides weak evidence against this mechanism but does not entirely exclude the broader thoracic outlet syndrome (B3) family given anatomic variant subtypes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Pattern of weakness following medial/lateral arm distributions?", "History of brachial plexus injury or repetitive overhead trauma?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Dynamic ultrasound of all three TOS variants (neurogenic, venous, arterial)", "CT angiography with contrast during arm elevation"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.7, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.35, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.1", "B2", "B5", "B3.3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 8, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the absence of viral/autoimmune triggers and presence of positional stability in symptoms contradict isolated reactive nerve injury as the mechanism?", "result_summary": "The absence of positional variation supports chronic processes over reactive mechanisms, moderately weakening B2 while having minimal impact on malignancy (B1) hypotheses.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "neutral", "B3.1": "neutral", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 9, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of reproducible pain with neck motion directly contradict the expected clinical features of scalenus anticus syndrome in weightlifters?", "result_summary": "Unreproducible scalenus signs (head-turning) contradict the expected clinical features of B3.1, but do not rule out the broader thoracic outlet family (B3) given uncertainty about anatomical variant subtypes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.1": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 10, "bundle_size": 11, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented symptom exacerbation with arm elevation contradict the typical presentation of subclavian steal syndrome?", "result_summary": "Absence of arm-elevation exacerbation (expected for B3.2) moderately weakens this diagnosis but preserves overall vascular compression (B3) plausibility through other subtypes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.2": "moderate_against", "B3.1": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 3, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the progressive motor-sensory deficit in the right arm with subacute onset and fixed pattern support combined thoracic outlet syndrome (B3.3) over arterial (B3.2) or neurogenic (B3.1) subtypes?", "result_summary": "The fixed neurological deficit without positional variation does not provide strong evidence for B3.3 over specific anatomic subtypes like B3.2, which would typically require positional testing confirmation.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3.3": "moderate_against", "B3.2": "neutral", "B3.1": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 3, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are there any findings in the vignette that definitively rule out mediastinal lymphoma (B1.2) despite the weight loss and smoking history?", "result_summary": "No direct evidence definitively excludes B1.2 lymphoma; the absence of systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma suspicion but does not eliminate the malignant process (B1)", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "weak_against", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 3, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the lack of a history of repetitive overhead motion or brachial plexus injury sufficient to contradict combined thoracic outlet syndrome (B3.3) as the mechanism for motor-sensory deficit?", "result_summary": "Absence of typical injury patterns for B3.3 provides weak evidence against this mechanism but does not entirely exclude the broader thoracic outlet syndrome (B3) family given anatomic variant subtypes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3": "neutral", "B3.3": "weak_against", "B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.4242424242424243, "B2": 0.18181818181818182, "B3": 0.24242424242424243, "B4": 0.030303030303030307, "B5": 0.12121212121212123