e trauma history or C8/T1 dermatomal patterns", "Diabetic mononeuropathy: Could explain unilateral symptoms but is less likely with concurrent pain and constitutional features"], "alarm_features": ["17 pound weight loss in 1 month", "Heavy alcohol consumption (2-7 drinks/day)", "Smoking 40 pack-years with apical risk implications"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Thoracic Malignancy with Neural Compression", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.349872224619163, "posterior": 0.5006568666768078, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute progression is atypical for embolic stroke and more consistent with inflammatory/malignant processes.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "evidence_against": ["No definitive signs of SVC syndrome or Cushingoid features observed, reducing but not eliminating concern for apical tumor."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of apical lung symptoms (cough, hoarseness)?", "Presence of superior vena cava syndrome?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Chest imaging (CT/MRI)", "Serum cancer markers"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neuromuscular Disorder of the Upper Extremity", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.021780316125731197, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of expected plexopathy patterns moderately disfavors this diagnosis."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Compression Syndrome of the Thoracic Outlet", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.06969566227473367, "posterior": 0.055315088573285584, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Fixed deficits with subacute onset are more characteristic of neurovascular compression (TOS) than isolated reactive nerve injury."], "evidence_against": ["Stable symptoms with head/neck movement and no anatomical risk markers (trauma, anomalies) contradict typical arterial TOS features.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of neck/shoulder trauma or anatomic anomalies?", "Pain changes with arm movement or scalenus muscle contraction?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Doppler ultrasound of subclavian artery", "Angiography of cervical/thoracic vessels"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Subacute Neurological Process with Ischemic Potential", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.014520210750487464, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Systemic Inflammatory/Reactive Nerve Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.05808084300194986, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Apical Lung Tumor with Truncal Compression (e.g., Pancoast Tumor)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3136304802363015, "posterior": 0.4704548283157938, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The presence of 17 pounds of weight loss, a history of anabolic steroid use for bodybuilding, and subacute progression provides moderate support for apical lung tumor/parietal syndrome, though confidence in exclusion of alternatives remains low.", "Constitutional symptoms and subacute neurologic defect maintain malignancy as a leading differential but reduce specificity for apical lung tumor."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of SVC syndrome signs contradicts a chronic apical lung presentation, slightly downgrading B1.1 while neutral for the broader B1 category since parietal mechanisms remain possible.", "Lack of typical upper extremity/neck radiation reduces but does not definitively exclude apical tumor."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of radiating arm pain or shoulder involvement?", "Cyanotic or edematous skin changes (superior mediastinal extension)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["High-resolution chest CT for apical mass with contrast", "PET scan for metabolic activity in parietacal space"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Mediastinal Lymphadenopathy from Lymphoma (Non-Hodgkin’s/Other)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.016262636040545963, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No direct evidence definitively excludes B1.2 lymphoma; the absence of systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma suspicion but does not eliminate the malignant process (B1)"]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Metastatic Thoracic Lesion (e.g., Neuroendocrine/Prostatic/Other)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.013939402320467965, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Anabolic steroid use, while not a direct carcinogen