y with contrast during arm elevation"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.7, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.35, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B3.3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 3, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the lack of a history of repetitive overhead motion or brachial plexus injury sufficient to contradict combined thoracic outlet syndrome (B3.3) as the mechanism for motor-sensory deficit?", "result_summary": "Absence of typical injury patterns for B3.3 provides weak evidence against this mechanism but does not entirely exclude the broader thoracic outlet syndrome (B3) family given anatomic variant subtypes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3": "neutral", "B3.3": "weak_against", "B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 17 lb weight loss, subacute progression, and absence of SVC syndrome reduce the likelihood of apical lung tumor (B1.1) and preserve malignancy (B1) family plausibility?", "result_summary": "Constitutional symptoms and subacute neurologic defect maintain malignancy as a leading differential but reduce specificity for apical lung tumor.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "strong_for", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Can the absence of radiating arm pain to the neck/spine definitively rule out Pancoast tumor (B1.1) despite constitutional symptoms?", "result_summary": "Lack of typical upper extremity