idence like trauma history or C8/T1 dermatomal patterns", "Diabetic mononeuropathy: Could explain unilateral symptoms but is less likely with concurrent pain and constitutional features"], "alarm_features": ["17 pound weight loss in 1 month", "Heavy alcohol consumption (2-7 drinks/day)", "Smoking 40 pack-years with apical risk implications"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Thoracic Malignancy with Neural Compression", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5006568666768078, "posterior": 0.4157890505667659, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute progression is atypical for embolic stroke and more consistent with inflammatory/malignant processes.", "Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."], "evidence_against": ["No definitive signs of SVC syndrome or Cushingoid features observed, reducing but not eliminating concern for apical tumor."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of apical lung symptoms (cough, hoarseness)?", "Presence of superior vena cava syndrome?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Chest imaging (CT/MRI)", "Serum cancer markers"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neuromuscular Disorder of the Upper Extremity", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.018088270761315223, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Weight loss and malignancy risk profile maintain apical lung tumor as a concerning possibility, but absence of SVC syndrome slightly reduces specificity for this variant without eliminating the broader B1 category."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Compression Syndrome of the Thoracic Outlet", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.04410092680853997, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Subacute Neurological Process with Ischemic Potential", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.014520210750487464, "posterior": 0.012058847174210147, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Fixed deficits without positional variation are less likely to represent cerebral infarction, more suggestive of chronic processes.", "Weight loss and malignancy risk profile maintain apical lung tumor as a concerning possibility, but absence of SVC syndrome slightly reduces specificity for this variant without eliminating the broader B1 category."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Any recent head/neck trauma or thromboembolic risk factors?", "History of transient ischemic attacks or focal neurologic symptoms?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Brain MRI with diffusion-weighted imaging", "Cardiac echo for source of emboli"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Systemic Inflammatory/Reactive Nerve Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.04823538869684059, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Apical Lung Tumor with Truncal Compression (e.g., Pancoast Tumor)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4704548283157938, "posterior": 0.3907066484444088, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and subacute neurologic defect maintain malignancy as a leading differential but reduce specificity for apical lung tumor.", "Weight loss and malignancy risk profile maintain apical lung tumor as a concerning possibility, but absence of SVC syndrome slightly reduces specificity for this variant without eliminating the broader B1 category."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of typical upper extremity/neck radiation reduces but does not definitively exclude apical tumor.", "Lack of radiation patterns reduces confidence in B1.1 as definitive cause but does not exclude it entirely since constitutional symptoms still favor the parent B1 malignancy branch."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of radiating arm pain or shoulder involvement?", "Cyanotic or edematous skin changes (superior mediastinal extension)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["High-resolution chest CT for apical mass with contrast", "PET scan for metabolic activity in parietacal space"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Mediastinal Lymphadenopathy from Lymphoma (Non-Hodgkin’s/Other)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.016262636040545963, "posterior": 0.013505908835115368, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Lack of constitutional symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma as the primary cause, moderately weakening B1.2 while having no material effect on B1.1 or other branches.", "No direct evidence definitively excludes B1.2 lymphoma; the absence of systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats) contradicts lymphoma suspicion but does not eliminate the malignant process (B1)"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Systemic symptoms (fevers, sweats, weight loss) consistent with lymphoma?", "History of prior lymphoproliferative illness?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Biopsy of enlarged mediastinal lymph nodes", "Flow cytometry of bone marrow aspirate"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Metastatic Thoracic Lesion (e.g., Neuroendocrine/Prostatic/Other)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.013939402320467965, "posterior": 0.011576493287241741, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Anabolic steroid use, while not a direct carcinogen, weakens the metastatic lesion hypothesis due to lack of documented primary tumor sites in the patient history."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Known primary cancer elsewhere in personal history (e.g., testes, GI tract)?", "Specific risk factors for cancer metastases (hormonal, paraneoplastic)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Whole-body bone scan for metastatic prostate cancer", "Testicular ultrasound considering steroid use history"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Scalenus Anticus Syndrome (Anatomical Variant Type)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.022969232712781236, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Unreproducible scalenus signs (head-turning) contradict the expected clinical features of B3.1, but do not rule out the broader thoracic outlet family (B3) given uncertainty about anatomical variant subtypes."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Subclavian Steal Syndrome (True Neurovascular Type)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.013781539627668739, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of arm-elevation exacerbation (expected for B3.2) moderately weakens this diagnosis but preserves overall vascular compression (B3) plausibility through other subtypes."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "Thoracic Outlet Syndrome (Non-specific/Combined Type)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.007350154468089996, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Positional neutrality doesn't rule out atypical B3 variants but strongly contradicts subtype-specific vascular theories (B3.2) while minimally affecting the broader B3 family."]}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.3", "B1.1", "B1.3", "B4", "B1.2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the anabolic steroid use and absence of autoimmune symptoms rule out systemic inflammatory/reactive nerve disease (B5) as the mechanism?", "result_summary": "Steroid use alone doesn't exclude reactive/inflammatory mechanisms without autoimmune features.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B5": "neutral", "B2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the fixed neurological pattern without anatomical injury trauma support non-specific thoracic outlet syndrome (B3.3) over subtype-specific mechanisms?", "result_summary": "Fixed deficits mildly weaken subtype-specific TOS (B3) but have limited impact on broader differentials.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3": "neutral", "B3.3": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 17-pound weight loss, subacute progression, and absence of superior vena cava syndrome (SVC) signs strongly favor apical lung tumor (B1.1) over other malignancy variants?", "result_summary": "Weight loss and malignancy risk profile maintain apical lung tumor as a concerning possibility, but absence of SVC syndrome slightly reduces specificity for this variant without eliminating the broader B1 category.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_for", "B1.1": "strong_for", "B2": "weak_against", "B3": "neutral", "B3.3": "weak_against", "B4": "weak_against", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the bodybuilder's physical activity patterns provide a plausible mechanism for non-specific thoracic outlet syndrome (B3.3), given the absence of anatomic injury or repetitive overhead motion history?", "result_summary": "Exercise-induced hypoperfusion is a potential pathophysiology, but bodybuilding history alone is insufficient to support B3.3 with current evidence.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_for", "B1.1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "mildly_weakened_subtypes", "B3.3": "weak_against", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the absence of typical apical tumor radiation patterns (shoulder/neck) sufficient to contradict B1.1 as the source of fixed bilateral deficits, especially given lack of metastatic workup findings?", "result_summary": "Lack of radiation patterns reduces confidence in B1.1 as definitive cause but does not exclude it entirely since constitutional symptoms still favor the parent B1 malignancy branch.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "moderate_against", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B3.3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of positional variability (unchanged with arm elevation) definitively exclude non-specific thoracic outlet syndrome (B3.3) as it weakens subtype-specific vascular theories?", "result_summary": "Positional neutrality doesn't rule out atypical B3 variants but strongly contradicts subtype-specific vascular theories (B3.2) while minimally affecting the broader B3 family.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "moderate_against", "B3.3": "weak_against", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.349872224619163, "B2": 0.052271746706050254, "B3": 0.06969566227473367, "B4": 0.017423915568683418, "B5": 0.06969566227473367, "B1.1": 0.3136304802363015, "B1.2": 0.019514785436925433, "B1.3": 0.01672695894593608, "B3.1": 0.033188410607016036, "B3.2": 0.019913046364209618, "B3.3": 0.016594205303508018}, {"B1": 0.5006568666768078, "B2": 0.021780316125731197, "B3": 0.055315088573285584, "B4": 0.014520210750487464, "B5": 0.05808084300194986, "B1.1": 0.4704548283157938, "B1.2": 0.016262636040545963, "B1.3": 0.013939402320467965, "B3.1": 0.027657544286642792, "B3.2": 0.016594526571985672, "B3.3": 0.011063017714657116}, {"B1": 0.4157890505667659, "B2": 0.018088270761315223, "B3": 0.04410092680853997, "B4": 0.012058847174210147, "B5": 0.04823538869684059, "B1.1": 0.3907066484444088, "B1.2": 0.013505908835115368, "B1.3": 0.011576493287241741, "B3.1": 0.022969232712781236, "B3.2": 0.013781539627668739, "B3.3": 0.007350154468089996}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Patient's vitals are stable (no shock, airway compromise, or severe respiratory distress). Neurological deficit is subacute with no acute stroke/TIA pattern evident from unchanged symptoms in positional testing. No signs of meningitis, tension pneumothorax, or active hemorrhage.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": true, "termination_type": "info_exhaustion", "reason": "turn budget reached"}, "turn_budget_used": 5, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.62, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.3907066484444088, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 55-year-old male bodybuilder presents to the emergency department with weakness of his right arm. The patient states he has experienced these symptoms for a few weeks; however, today his hand felt so weak he dropped his cup of tea. The patient has a medical history of diabetes. He drinks 2-7 alcoholic drinks per day and has smoked 2 packs of cigarettes per day since he was 25. The patient uses anabolic steroids. He has lost 17 pounds since he last came to the emergency department 1 month ago. His temperature is 99.5°F (37.5°C), blood pressure is 177/108 mmHg, pulse is 90/min, respirations are 17/min, and oxygen saturation is 98% on room air. Physical exam reveals decreased sensation in the right arm and 2/5 strength in the right arm and 5/5 strength in the left arm. The patient states that he is experiencing a dull aching and burning pain in his right arm during the exam. Symptoms are not changed with changes in head and neck position.", "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Apical lung tumor"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Brachial plexopathy"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Cerebral infarction"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Scalenus anticus syndrome"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Subclavian steal syndrome"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "conte